# CORE PHYSICS: the files the git hooks and the weekly check treat as core.
#
# Core = Hamiltonian construction, circuit sampling, QSCI subspace selection
# and diagonalization, GQE loss and updates. Everything else (plotting, I/O,
# configs, job scripts, utilities) is not core.
#
# One repo-relative path per line. A trailing "/" means everything under that
# directory; otherwise the line must match a file exactly. "#" starts a comment.
# This file is the single place the boundary is defined: edit it here, and the
# hooks and the weekly check follow.

# Hamiltonian construction
gqe_qsci/molecule.py

# operators and circuit sampling
gqe_qsci/gqe/operator_pool.py
gqe_qsci/gqe/utils.py
gqe_qsci/gqe/sampler.py
hpc/numpy_sampler.py

# QSCI: subspace selection, diagonalization, refinement, classical baselines
gqe_qsci/qsci/

# GQE loss and updates (training_step and the rollout/reward path live in
